---
description: UI/UX standards for components and pages
globs: src/app/**/*.tsx,src/components/**/*.tsx
---

This is how we compete on UX — hold this bar:

- **Mobile-first.** Design the 375px layout first, then enhance with `sm:`/`md:`/`lg:`.
  Tap targets ≥ 40px, no horizontal overflow.
- **shadcn = Base UI.** For polymorphism use `render`, e.g.
  `<Button render={<Link href="/x" />}>Label</Button>` — `asChild` does not exist here.
- **Design tokens only.** `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`,
  `border-border`, `bg-primary`, … never raw hex/`zinc-900`. Must look correct in light & dark.
- **Every async surface needs loading + empty + error states.** `Skeleton` for loading,
  a real empty state, inline errors, and `toast` (sonner) for action feedback.
- **Accessibility:** semantic elements, labelled inputs, visible focus, keyboard nav,
  `aria-label` on meaning-bearing icon buttons.
- **Motion is subtle** (`motion`): micro-interactions only, no layout shift, respect
  `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Reuse existing `src/components/ui/*`; add new primitives via `npx shadcn@latest add <name>`,
  don't hand-roll them.
- Keep components small; lift data fetching to Server Components and logic to `src/lib`.
